# scratch/ is a workbench, not part of the project: vendor repos, sample
# models, downloaded reference code, host-side experiments and build output.
# About 1.5 GB of it, none of it version-controlled by design.
#
# One consequence worth knowing: the UI asset generator
# (scratch/gen_ui_assets.py) and the designer's source artwork live there,
# so they are NOT in this repository. That does not affect building - its
# output, sessions/session_13/FSBL/Inc/ui/ui_assets.{h,inc}, IS committed,
# and a fresh clone builds and flashes without it. It only matters if you
# want to regenerate the sprites and fonts from the original PNGs.
/scratch/
